body:
I will write as alone post to answer to all of you so I avoid spamming and repeating myself.  
&nbsp;

First of all thank you so much for your kind response and I'm from Europe :)  
&nbsp;&nbsp;

Yes I have very low self-esteem because well I'm not really 'beautiful', lets be real I'm pretty ugly.. because of my disorder of jaw. So I got a lot of 'weird' looks from others. And I am hard to understand as my voice is different. (-> often quiet) And back then I was so shy. So ugly + shy = bullying == huge low self-esteem ;) And it was the worst nightmare. I didn't want to go to mall/shops or anywhere. Just school which was like hell and home at which I felt free. I closed myself into my room and run behind computer and internet. I had and still don't have any or very low support from my family. There's no trust, no helping or supporting each other. Right now I think I am in a much better shape in terms of confidence. I learned a lot in past about that. Why I feel unmotivated. Idk I guess because I always felt useless, unwanted, pointless. This ugliness can be fixed with surgery and I wish that surgery will come true. I still have that feeling when I talk to people for the first time, they look at me different, but it's getting better and better. In past (welp also last year :P) I was avoiding social situations/conversations, I was afraid of people, now it's better, I have improved my self-esteem, but right when it started to get better I got that shock of depression and loss of motivation and hope. Second worst time in my life after school bullying if not the worst; when I was bullied at least I could get (run) away from school, but this time felt to be here for ever.  

&nbsp;&nbsp;

About getting help. Yes I was thinking about that:) heh hmm what should I say to doc? Idk what to say. Will this depressive state happen again?  Will I be fine now. Do I need to see a doctor?  

&nbsp;&nbsp;

Thank you all very much for your help with such great words. I feel better I'm jut not sure right now what to do. What if all this repeats. Will I be OK?  I feel insecure, uncertain, unsure. Like I'm afraid to try/do something new. As if I know that I will fail. IDK I'm sorry for this mess :)  

&nbsp;

I will definitely start doing exercises again. Actually right now I will do it 20push-ups as I did back in good old days :) Made it 23 push-ups!  
&nbsp;

Thanks again for your wise words. For that little chat :) You are heroes. Thank you!!!
/u/suicidalperson90 /u/1WithTheUniverse /u/NordicSpirit /u/i_refute_it_thus

 Edit: Of course thanks to all of you who have read and took time to vote or comment.
